course: dictionary
lesson: 1170
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning, and the context tells you which one you need. «The match will be broadcast live on television tonight.» Here broadcast means sent out as a programme for people to watch.
explain: «Don't broadcast it» means don't tell lots of people a secret. The same word now means something different. The clue is that the thing being told is private, so it is not about a television.
explain: Broadcast can also be a noun, a thing you can name. «The evening news broadcast starts at six.» The broadcast is the programme itself. Check by swapping in a word like programme: if it still makes sense, you have the right meaning.
fact: Broadcast means to send out a programme on TV, radio or the internet.
fact: A broadcast is a programme sent out on TV, radio or online.
fact: «Broadcast» can also mean telling lots of people news or a secret, as in «don't broadcast it».
fact: A broadcast sends the same message from one sender to many listeners at once, while «a phone call goes from one person to another».
fact: Long ago, farmers broadcast seeds, scattering them widely by hand.
exercise: «The match will be broadcast live on television.» What does broadcast mean here? | To switch the television off | To whisper a secret to one friend | To scatter seeds by hand | *To send out a programme for people to watch
exercise: Maya tells her friend, «Don't broadcast it», about a secret. What does she mean? | Don't send it by post | Don't write it down in a notebook | Don't turn the television on | *Don't tell lots of people
exercise: In «The evening news broadcast starts at six», what is a broadcast? | *A programme sent out on TV or radio | A type of seed | A loud shout in the playground | A phone call between two people
test: «A 90-minute broadcast starts at 7:15.» When does it end? | 8:05 | 9:15 | *8:45 | 8:15
test: «A broadcast, like radio or TV, goes from one sender to many listeners; a phone call goes from one person to another.» What is the difference? | A broadcast reaches one person, while a phone call reaches many | Both reach many people at once | Neither one sends a message | *A broadcast reaches many listeners, while a phone call reaches one person
exam: Each sprite has its own scripts, but a sprite can send a message to all the others with «broadcast». What does broadcast mean here? | To delete a script | *To send a message out to many sprites at once | To scatter seeds across a field | To keep a message secret from everyone
